    title: "CISA與FBI發出警告：2026年美國中期選舉期間，選舉與競選人員面臨網路威脅",
    summary: "美國網路安全和基礎設施安全局（CISA）與聯邦調查局（FBI）共同發布了公共服務公告（PSA），警告所有選舉和競選相關人員，關於2026年美國中期選舉期間可能面臨的網路威脅。文章指出，惡意網路行為者可能會利用高度複雜的網路釣魚（phishing）和簡訊釣魚（smishing）技術，竊取登入憑證或敏感資訊，甚至在目標設備上植入惡意軟體。由於選舉官員、候選人及政黨組織掌握著選民登記資料、現任政府官員資訊和敏感競選資料，這些群體成為了極具吸引力的攻擊目標。攻擊者可能會設計出極度逼真、難以辨識的電子郵件、簡訊、音訊或影片內容，旨在操縱接收者洩露敏感資訊或點擊惡意連結。CISA和FBI呼籲相關人員和公眾務必審閱此公告，並提高警覺，留意可疑的電子郵件和行動訊息，採取適當的網路安全防護措施。",
    tags: ["CISA", "FBI", "網路釣魚", "Smishing", "選舉安全", "2026 U.S. midterm elections"],
    title_en: "CISA and FBI Issue Warning: Election and Campaign Personnel Face Cyber Threats During 2026 U.S. Midterm Elections",
    summary_en: "The Cybersecurity and Infrastructure Security Agency (CISA) and the Federal Bureau of Investigation (FBI) jointly issued a Public Service Announcement (PSA) warning all election and campaign personnel about potential cyber threats during the 2026 U.S. midterm elections. The article notes that malicious actors may utilize highly sophisticated phishing and smishing techniques to steal login credentials or sensitive information, or even implant malware on target devices. Because election officials, candidates, and political party organizations possess voter registration data, information on current government officials, and sensitive campaign materials, these groups are highly attractive targets. Attackers may design extremely realistic and difficult-to-detect emails, text messages, audio, or video content, aimed at manipulating recipients into divulging sensitive information or clicking malicious links. CISA and FBI urge relevant personnel and the public to review this announcement, raise their awareness, and be vigilant regarding suspicious emails and mobile messages, taking appropriate cybersecurity measures.",
