    title_en: "Apple Updates App Store Guidelines: Strengthening Review and Restrictions on AI-Generated Content, Hidden Features, and Inappropriate Content",
    summary_en: "Apple recently updated its App Review Guidelines to strengthen the review process for harmful content and deceptive application behavior within the App Store. This update primarily focuses on three areas: First, regarding user-generated content, it explicitly mandates that developers must prevent issues such as copyright infringement, nonconsensual intimate imagery, and anonymous bullying, warning that failure to remedy violations may constitute a breach of the Developer Program Guidelines. Second, Apple significantly tightened rules concerning \"bait-and-switch\" applications, adding provisions that strictly prohibit developers from including any hidden, dormant, or undocumented features in the App Store. It specifically targets behaviors that conceal features through methods like code obfuscation, with violations potentially leading to app removal or developer account termination. Finally, in the legal section, Apple also reinforced mechanisms for removing and blocking applications that assist in human trafficking or child exploitation. These changes reflect Apple's stricter management approach to addressing AI-generated content (such as \"nudification\") and malicious application behavior.",
    tags_en: ["Apple", "App Store", "App Review Guidelines", "AI-Generated Content", "Hidden Features", "nonconsensual intimate imagery"],
