    summary_en: "This article compares two flagship models Apple is set to launch: the iPhone Duo (foldable screen) and the iPhone 18 Pro (traditional model). The two devices exhibit significant differences in appearance, screen, camera, and features. The iPhone Duo adopts a foldable design, featuring a 5.4-inch outer screen and a 7.6-inch foldable inner screen, and introduces the nano-texture finish for the first time. Regarding cameras, the iPhone 18 Pro boasts a 48MP main camera with a variable aperture and a unique Telephoto camera, significantly leading in photographic capabilities. Furthermore, the iPhone 18 Pro exclusively supports professional features such as ProRes video recording, Spatial Video, and Genlock. In terms of authentication, the iPhone Duo uses Touch ID, while the iPhone 18 Pro retains Face ID. For battery life, the iPhone 18 Pro Max claims up to 45 hours, while the iPhone Duo's battery life varies depending on the screen used. In terms of pricing, the iPhone Duo starts at $1,999, and the iPhone 18 Pro starts at $1,199. Users are advised to choose the model that best suits their needs based on whether they require a foldable screen experience, professional photography features, or their budget.",
