    summary_en: "This article shares a personal review of the iPhone 18 Pro after approximately one month of use, focusing primarily on three impressive feature upgrades. First is the battery life; the author notes that even with daily use, the phone retains about 60% charge by evening, suggesting a significant improvement in Apple's battery technology this year. Second is the variable aperture main camera, which the author points out produces excellent photos even in 'Auto' mode, without needing professional settings. The third point is the cooling effect of the vapor chamber cooling system. The author mentions that in outdoor or strong sunlight environments, the iPhone 18 Pro remains sufficiently cool, preventing performance slowdowns due to overheating and thus enhancing the overall user experience. Overall, the article emphasizes the comprehensive optimization of the iPhone 18 Pro in terms of battery, photography, and thermal management.",
