    summary_en: "OpenAI recently announced a deep integration of ChatGPT with the Google Chrome browser. This feature allows ChatGPT not only to provide contextually relevant answers based on the content of open browser tabs but also to directly control these tabs to execute various tasks. Specific applications include: comparing product specifications across multiple tabs (such as sofa dimensions or materials), drafting comparative reports based on multiple page contents, filling out forms, downloading files, and even helping users organize and group large numbers of tabs. Furthermore, the integration provides a sidebar user interface (UI) similar to the built-in Gemini interface in Chrome. This extension is currently available on the Chrome Web Store. This move indicates that AI assistants are moving toward deeper browser control layers, enhancing the practicality of AI in daily web information processing and task automation.",
