    summary_en: "This article reports on several recent key developments in the space industry. Japan's Mars Moon eXploration (MMX) mission is scheduled to use Japan's H3 rocket to explore Mars's moons, Phobos and Deimos. In terms of commercial launches, California startup Reflect Orbital announced the purchase of two launch services from India's Skyroot Aerospace, utilizing the Vikram-1 and upgraded Vikram-1U rockets, respectively. Reflect Orbital's business model involves deploying a satellite constellation containing approximately 50,000 mirrors to transmit solar energy from orbit to Earth for power generation and illumination. The company's choice of the Indian market reflects industry concerns regarding potential supply shortages in US launch capabilities, especially as SpaceX transitions away from the Falcon 9 toward Starship. Furthermore, LEAP, a startup based in Colorado, is also targeting the small satellite launch market. Its Bighorn rocket is designed for dedicated launch services in low Earth orbit (LEO), with its first launch targeted for 2028.",
